// kyoten::frame::Camera — a view of the world, drawn for a player (the first slice's step 9, KYR-9; rendering.md
// § Decided, 2026-11-07, question 2's first cut, and 2026-11-27, step 9's two questions and its kyoten half; input.md
// § Decided, 2026-11-26, the sixth part's question 1). Its records require a `Transform`: the camera is where its
// entity is, looking along its own −Z, y up, as three.js's, Bevy's and Godot's cameras look.
//
// - `player` is the player it is drawn for, numbered from 1, and `view` which of the game's views it is (the generated
//   `Views`), -1 naming none. What the platform drew comes back as the view's `DrawnView`, which turns the cursor for a
//   binding that names the view.
// - `fov` is the vertical field of view in degrees, and `near` and `far` the planes, in metres.
// - `exposure` is in EV100, as Filament, Bevy, Unreal and `@kama/graphics` set it: the scene's linear light is scaled by
//   2^−EV100 / 1.2. Its default is three.js's exposure of 1, −log2(1.2), so a light of intensity 1 looks as it does
//   there; sunlight is about 15, indoors about 7.
// - `toneMapping` is how the light is brought into the display's range, each camera its own.
//
// It offers what `@kama/graphics` draws: a perspective camera over the whole window. An orthographic camera (GFX-7) and
// a view drawn into part of the window or a texture each join with the row that draws them.
//
// The frame tier's, beside `DrawnView`, since the frame-tier render list carries it as it is (step 9's kyoten half,
// question 1).

export { Camera, ToneMapping };

// A camera's tone mapping, read and written by its case name, as `@kama/graphics` offers it: `None`, the light clamped;
// `AgX`, Troy Sobotka's curve; `BlenderAgX`, Blender's AgX with its look, the library's default.
@generate(Serializable, Deserializable)
type enum ToneMapping { None, AgX, BlenderAgX }

@generate(Serializable, Deserializable)
type value Camera {
    @field public int32 player = 1;
    @field public int32 view = -1;
    @field public float32 fov = 60.0;
    @field public float32 near = 0.1;
    @field public float32 far = 1000.0;
    @field public float32 exposure = -0.2630344058;
    @field public ToneMapping toneMapping = ToneMapping::BlenderAgX;

    // Player 1's, naming no view: 60 degrees, from 0.1 m to 1 km, three.js's exposure of 1 and Blender's AgX.
    public default ctor make() { }
}
